          "rule_number": 152
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "target_argument_id": "arg_45b6c4dd",
      "ground": "The argument conflates the 'knew or should have known' standard of Article 28(a) with the distinct 'consciously disregarded' standard required for non-military superiors under Article 28(b).",
      "reasoning": "The officer is described as a civilian Chief of Staff/Deputy Commander, not a 'military commander or person effectively acting as a military commander' in the direct sense of 28(a). For such superiors, Article 28(b)(i) requires that the superior 'knew, or consciously disregarded information which clearly indicated' the crimes. The argument relies on the lower threshold of 'should have known' from 28(a), which does not apply to the legal characterization of a civilian superior's liability under 28(b).",
      "severity": "material",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "rome_statute",
          "article": "28(b)(i)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "target_argument_id": "arg_a65f7313",
      "ground": "The argument misstates the legal standard for 'punishment' in command responsibility by ignoring the specific requirement to 'submit the matter to competent authorities' as an alternative to direct punishment.",
      "reasoning": "Article 28(b)(iii) and 28(a)(ii) require measures to 'prevent or repress their commission or to submit the matter to the competent authorities for investigation and prosecution.' The facts state the officer instructed cooperation with an investigation already underway by the 6th Corps Security Service. The argument fails to address whether this constituted a failure to 'submit the matter to competent authorities,' which is a valid discharge of the duty under the Statute, rather than asserting a requirement for direct punishment which is not the only legal standard.",
      "severity": "minor",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "rome_statute",
          "article": "28(b)(iii)"
